From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:55:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] windows.web: HttpContent.Headers and typed content header
 values (3290)

Implements HttpContent.Headers (it was E_NOTIMPL, escalated because the
IHttpContentHeaderCollection IID and layout were thought missing: both are in
windows-rs 0.58.0 Windows.Web.Http.Headers, used as data only).

New http_content_headers.c:
- HttpContentHeaderCollection (activatable) with the typed face
  (ContentDisposition, ContentEncoding, ContentLanguage, ContentLength,
  ContentLocation, ContentMD5, ContentRange, ContentType, Expires,
  LastModified, Append, TryAppendWithoutValidation) plus IMap<HSTRING,HSTRING>
  (Lookup/Insert/Remove/Clear/HasKey/Size/GetView), IIterable of key/value
  pairs and IStringable ("Name: value" lines).
- Typed header values as activatable classes with factories and
  Parse/TryParse statics: HttpMediaTypeHeaderValue, HttpContentDisposition-
  HeaderValue, HttpContentRangeHeaderValue, HttpContentCodingHeaderValue,
  HttpNameValueHeaderValue; Parameters is a real IVector of name/value
  objects; the language and coding collections have ParseAdd/TryParseAdd.
- The typed objects stay live: changing the object changes the header.
- HttpContent.Headers returns the collection (Content-Type seeded, Content-
  Length computed from the body when read). HttpStringContent now sets
  "text/plain; charset=utf-8" by default and encodes UTF-16 bodies.
- The transport sends the content headers set by the app, and the content of
  a response carries the Content-* / Expires / Last-Modified headers it got.

